#edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259612 #edb/ref 1071 "If ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=15$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=10,$ calculate ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259612 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "caa68865-4fa8-5716-bcf1-19dd497b3997" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259612 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 15 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 15 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x-10 \\\\ 25 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-25.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259614 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259433 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259614 #edb/ref 1069 "q-124186" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259614 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259614 #edb/ref 1071 "If ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=16$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=11,$ calculate ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259614 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7673d1a0-afd2-5d22-93cd-75c43bd54a25" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259614 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -{\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -16 & =-11+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -5 & ={\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-5.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259615 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259079 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259615 #edb/ref 1069 "q-124188" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259615 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259615 #edb/ref 1071 "If ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=21,$ ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=2,$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-11,$ calculate ${\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259615 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8ad1a2a8-0a25-5345-b64f-001fe66a3826" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259615 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -{\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & =2-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -21 & =2-(-11)+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -21 & =13+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -34 & ={\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-34.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259670 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259183 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259670 #edb/ref 1069 "q-124334" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259670 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259670 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/9c/9c42d875a65a6b54ad7769180f5ec2e831772ad44a89ec913951da40c6d90514.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path along the line segment between the points $(-3,0)$ to the point $(0,2),$ as shown above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259670 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "19da757c-af27-523a-9d2f-9ce008944b1f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259670 #edb/ref 1074 "The line integral of unity with respect to $y$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $y$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{2}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${y}_{1}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{2}=2$ and ${y}_{1}=0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1}=2-0=2.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259671 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259374 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259671 #edb/ref 1069 "q-124335" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259671 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259671 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/96/963f8812eb8226617c7d893ebdf675747ebed12c92